<sect1 id="wine" xreflabel="Wine-&wine-version;">
  <?dbhtml filename="wine.html"?>

  <title>Wine-&wine-version;</title>

  <indexterm zone="wine">
    <primary sortas="a-wine">wine</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <sect2 role="package">
    <title>Introduction to Wine</title>

    <para>
      Wine is a compatibility layer for running Windows programs on Unix.
    </para>

    <note><para>
      You do not have to rebuild <xref linkend="dxvk"/> or <xref
      linkend="vkd3d-proton"/> after updating Wine. This is because those
      packages build against the MinGW-w64 static libraries built in that
      package, and not against the DLLs provided in this package. When you
      update this package, you don't have to worry about much else beyond maybe
      having to download mono again, which is handled automatically whenever
      you execute Wine after updating.
    </para></note>

    &long-build-time;

    <itemizedlist spacing="compact">
      <listitem>
        <para>
          Download: <ulink url="&wine-download;"/>
        </para>
      </listitem>
    </itemizedlist>

